{
 "title": "Why the sky should be purple",
 "sentences": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "display": "Why is the sky blue?",
   "pauseBefore": 0,
   "title": true,
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.109
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "display": "Plot twist: it should be PURPLE.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 1.409,
   "end": 2.977
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "display": "Most people think it's reflecting the ocean.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.55,
   "start": 3.527,
   "end": 5.779
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "display": "It's not.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 6.079,
   "end": 6.758
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "display": "Look up at noon: blue.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.5,
   "start": 7.258,
   "end": 8.479
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "display": "Look up at sunset: orange.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.35,
   "start": 8.829,
   "end": 10.379
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "display": "Stand on the Moon: pitch black.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.35,
   "start": 10.729,
   "end": 12.325
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "display": "But look at what's actually happening.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.5,
   "start": 12.825,
   "end": 14.502
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "display": "Sunlight is every colour mixed together.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 14.802,
   "end": 16.753
  },
  {
   "n": 10,
   "display": "When it hits the tiny molecules in our air, short waves get bounced everywhere.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.35,
   "start": 17.103,
   "end": 21.699
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "display": "Blue scatters about six times more than red.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.35,
   "start": 22.049,
   "end": 24.312
  },
  {
   "n": 12,
   "display": "That's RAYLEIGH SCATTERING.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.75,
   "concept": true,
   "start": 25.062,
   "end": 26.229
  },
  {
   "n": 13,
   "display": "Violet scatters even more.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.55,
   "start": 26.779,
   "end": 28.324
  },
  {
   "n": 14,
   "display": "But the Sun sends less of it, and your eyes are bad at seeing it.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 28.624,
   "end": 32.039
  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "display": "So your brain settles on blue.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 32.339,
   "end": 33.872
  },
  {
   "n": 16,
   "display": "At sunset, light crosses so much air that the blue gets scattered away first.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.45,
   "start": 34.322,
   "end": 38.673
  },
  {
   "n": 17,
   "display": "Only orange and red make it through.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 38.973,
   "end": 40.691
  },
  {
   "n": 18,
   "display": "And the Moon has no air at all, so *nothing* scatters.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.45,
   "start": 41.141,
   "end": 43.838
  },
  {
   "n": 19,
   "display": "So the sky you see isn't the real colour.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.5,
   "start": 44.338,
   "end": 46.375
  },
  {
   "n": 20,
   "display": "It's your eyes making a deal.",
   "pauseBefore": 0.3,
   "start": 46.675,
   "end": 48.056
  },
  {
   "n": 21,
   "display": "Next time someone asks why the sky is blue\u2026",
   "pauseBefore": 0.7,
   "start": 48.756,
   "end": 51.049
  }
 ],
 "voice": "Kokoro TTS v1.0, am_fenrir, speed 1.0"
}